 management overlays, increasing the buffer to INR50 crores. The company remains on track to achieve its long-term consolidated AUM target of INR32,000 crores by FY2030, with 30% coming from non-microfinance businesses. Additionally, the promoter group infused INR100 crores through warrants, with the first tranche of INR25 crores already received. Satin Creditcare Network Limited reported strong financial and operational results for the quarter and half year ended September 30, 2026, highlighting growth in AUM, disbursements, and profitability across standalone and consolidated entities.","themes":{"guidance":[{"claim":"The company expects to land within the guided consolidated AUM growth range of 20% to 25% for the full year.","quote":"On consolidated AUM growth, we guided 20% to 25% for the full year. We have grown 9% in the first half, which annualizes to roughly 19%. We are approaching the range rather than inside it and we want to be straightforward about that. The second half is seasonally a stronger period for disbursement, and on the basis of our current pipeline, we expect to land within the guided range for the full year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Management guided a standalone credit cost range of 3% to 3.5% for FY27.","quote":"On standalone credit cost, we guided 3% to 3.5%. We are at 2.8% for the half year, and that is after adding to our overlay rather than releasing it. We are ahead.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Management guided a standalone return on assets of 3.5% to 4% for FY27.","quote":"On standalone return on asset, we guided 3.5% to 4%. We are at 4.3% for the half year on a reported basis, which is above the top of the range even after absorbing the INR50 crores buffer, we are ahead.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"The company targeted consolidated AUM growth of 20 to 25% for FY27.","quote":"Consolidated AUM Growth 20–25%","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Standalone credit cost guidance for FY27 was set at 3.0 to 3.5%.","quote":"Standalone Credit Cost 3.0–3.5%","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Standalone ROA guidance for FY27 was established at 3.5 to 4.0%.","quote":"Standalone ROA 3.5–4.0%","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Consolidated AUM was targeted to reach ₹32,000 Crores by FY-2030.","quote":"Consolidated AUM targeted to reach ₹32,000 Crores by FY-2030 : 52% of the Target Achieved","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Management projects a stand-alone credit cost of 3% to 3.5% for FY27.","quote":"Stand-alone credit cost of 3% to 3.5% on a reported basis.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The company targets a stand-alone return on assets of 3.5% to 4% for FY27.","quote":"And stand-alone return on assets of 3.5% to 4%, again on a reported basis.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"}],"demand_outlook":[{"claim":"Management noted that rural cash flow recovery following the monsoon has been very encouraging.","quote":"We had earlier indicated that the revised outlook warranted caution on rural cash flows over the subsequent two to three months. That period has now passed and the recovery has now been very encouraging.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"The company has not witnessed any stress in repayment in Karnataka and Maharashtra.","quote":"Also, as of now, we have not witnessed any stress in repayment in these states.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Management noted that the second half of the year has seasonally higher growth.","quote":"*H2 has seasonally higher growth","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Management noted that the industry has transitioned from a phase of repair to expansion.","quote":"As for the sector, we can say with confidence that the industry has moved from repair to expansion.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The company is monitoring rural cash flows due to the revised monsoon outlook.","quote":"The revised monsoon outlook warrants caution on rural cash flows over the next 2 to 3 months.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"}],"capex_expansion":[{"claim":"Satin Finserv added 19 branches during the quarter, bringing its total to 140 branches across 16 states.","quote":"Satin Finserv continues to be the standout with AUM of INR1,761 crores, up 184% year-on-year and 29% sequentially, now across 140 branches in 116 states with 19 branches added during the quarter.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Satin Housing Finance operates across 59 branches in 22 states.","quote":"Satin Housing Finance stands at INR1,219 crores, up 19% year- on- year, with CRAR at 57.67% and gearing at 1.70x across 59 branches in 22 states and net worth of INR370 crores.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"The company commenced operations in Kerala in June.","quote":"In June, we commenced operations in Kerala, strengthening our South India presence alongside Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, Andhra Pradesh and Telangana","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"}],"margins_costs":[{"claim":"The company's operating expense ratio was 6.6% compared to 7.2% a year ago.","quote":"Our operating expense ratio was 6.6% against 7.2% a year ago.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Cost-to-income improved to 41.6% from 49.8%.","quote":"Cost-to-income improved to 41.6% from 49.8%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"The marginal cost of borrowing reduced by 65 basis points year-on-year to 10.28%.","quote":"Our marginal cost of borrowing reduced by 65 basis points year-on-year to 10.28%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Marginal borrowing cost reduced by 65 bps year-over-year to 10.28% in Q2FY27.","quote":"Marginal borrowing cost reduced by 65bps YoY to 10.28% in Q2FY27.","doc_kind":"concall_ppt","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=3fef86b5-a74d-460a-bd69-5cfa8c2684c7.pdf"},{"claim":"Stand-alone NIM improved to 14.36% during the quarter.","quote":"On margins and efficiency, stand-alone NIM improved to 14.36% from 13.16% on gross yield of 22.44% against a cost of funds of 8.08%.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The operating expense ratio improved to 6.33% as branches added last year seasoned.","quote":"Our operating expense ratio improved to 6.33% from 6.98% in Q4 as the 392 branches added last year begin to season.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"}],"orders_capacity":[{"claim":"Standalone AUM stood at INR13,608 crores, representing a 23% year-on-year increase.","quote":"Standalone AUM stood at INR13,608 crores, up 23% year- on- year.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-11-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=be7c3201-4574-4679-ada9-0b7bc508b60a.pdf"},{"claim":"Consolidated AUM reached INR15,935 crores, growing 27% year-on-year.","quote":"Consolidated AUM reached INR15,935 crores, growing 27% year-on-year and 5% sequentially.","doc_kind":"concall_transcript","doc_date":"2026-08-01","url":"https://www.bseindia.com/stockinfo/AnnPdfOpen.aspx?Pname=90c3b889-651a-41e1-9e47-a07047397bb2.pdf"},{"claim":"The company serves 34 lakh clients across 2,041 branches.","quote":"We serve 34 lakh 